named a false culprit.

32
00:02:55,829 --> 00:03:02,036
And this one it first got wrong — it
abstained where a real answer existed.

33
00:03:02,116 --> 00:03:07,909
I found the seam, fixed it, and left the
original failure in the repo.

34
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:14,978
Run it twice. Same input, same seed, same
verdict hash.

35
00:03:15,058 --> 00:03:20,023
There is no LLM anywhere in the runtime —
this is deterministic.

36
00:03:20,103 --> 00:03:25,069
The corpus is synthetic and disclosed;
ground truth comes from a manifest.

37
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:40,492
And you don't need my machine to check any
of it.

38
00:03:40,572 --> 00:03:46,779
The whole run is stepped through in the
browser — the board, the compiled query,

39
00:03:46,859 --> 00:03:50,169
